1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,076
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,126 --> 00:00:05,844
Junior Makers, video 2.

3
00:00:05,894 --> 00:00:08,370
Power, path and load.

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:13,820
Every simple circuit has a power source, a path of wires, and

5
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:16,440
a load — the part that does the work.

6
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:20,188
The battery provides power.

7
00:00:20,238 --> 00:00:22,031
Wires make the path.

8
00:00:22,081 --> 00:00:27,100
An LED or buzzer is the load that does the useful work.

9
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:31,257
A closed path lets the load run.

10
00:00:31,307 --> 00:00:34,829
An open path has a gap, so nothing runs.

11
00:00:34,879 --> 00:00:38,400
An unplugged wire means an open circuit.

12
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,345
Let us recap.

13
00:00:41,395 --> 00:00:45,485
Power, path and load make a circuit.

14
00:00:45,535 --> 00:00:48,360
Open circuits do not run.

15
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:50,200
Next: Stay safe.
